## 1) Migrate (CAP-G6 soft leftover close)

### Before (SOFT_LEGACY — peer1)

```
fn resolve_ipv4(net: &NetCap, hostname: String) -> Result[String, String]
```

Class: **SOFT_LEGACY** — NetCap on soft-granular UDP residual string; **not** raw. Prefer UdpCap.

### After (this integration)

```
fn resolve_ipv4(udp: &UdpCap, hostname: String) -> Result[String, String]
    requires hostname != ""
{
    if hostname == "localhost" {
        return Ok("127.0.0.1");
    }
    return Err("Residual: UDP socket DNS not implemented");
}
```

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Preferred formal | **`&UdpCap`** |
| Param name | `udp` (was `net`) |
| Sealed ops used | **none** (no `bind_udp` / `udp_recv` call yet) |
| Body honesty | localhost → `Ok("127.0.0.1")`; else residual Err |
| Header honesty | CAP-G6 UdpCap preferred; not raw/L2; residual UDP DNS not implemented |

### verify block note

Product has **no `UdpCap(0)` ctor** for verify harnesses (`oodac check` → `undefined variable 'UdpCap'`). Verify keeps **`NetCap(0)`** call sites so residual behavior stays asserted under **soft-granular supersede** (legacy NetCap still supersedes UdpCap at check — CAP-G1 one-wave). Formal remains preferred **`&UdpCap`**.

